.TH MDT.EXPORTS.CLEAR 4 2026-09-08 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.exports.clear, obdfilter.exports.clear \- clear per-NID export statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME "*.exports.clear=" VALUE
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param obdfilter." FSNAME "*.exports.clear=" VALUE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT and OST device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writing any value to
.B exports.clear
resets the statistics of every NID currently active on the device, and also
immediately evicts every per-NID statistics structure that is idle (has no
active exports), regardless of how long it has been idle - unlike the
background scanner controlled by
.BR nid_stats_idle_time (4),
which only evicts entries older than its configured timeout.
.PP
The value written is not otherwise interpreted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Clear all NID statistics on every MDT of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl set_param mdt.testfs-*.exports.clear=1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B mdt.exports.clear
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.58
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.nid_stats_idle_time (4),
.BR lustre (7),
.BR lctl (8)
